The attached image, Fig. 5, illustrates how Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes and uptake by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). Panel A displays flow cytometry plots showing that both aluminum hydroxide (AH) and Nano-11 adjuvants increase the number of OVA-containing APCs compared to OVA alone. Panel B quantifies the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in these cells, indicating that Nano-11 leads to significantly greater per-cell antigen uptake than AH. Panel C shows that Nano-11 also significantly increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells in the lymph nodes, especially on Day 2, suggesting targeted delivery to these immunopotentiating cells.